  "body": "Evidence-only for OMN-21150. Touches no runtime path: the diff is `contracts/OMN-21150.yaml` only.\n\nAdds two dod_evidence items, binding AC1 and AC2, and their acceptance records under `context.ac_binding_provenance`. Proposed by `lane=dod-closeout-bind-2026-11-16T2345Z-c2`; accepted by `lane=dod-closeout-accept-2026-11-16T2345Z-c2`. The criterion hashes are taken over the live ticket criteria with `omnimarket.occ_contract_pin.criterion_hash`. As a positive control, the same function reproduces the AC3 hash recorded in `contracts/OMN-21143.yaml`.\n\n- AC1: `tests/nodes/node_hybrid_codegen_orchestrator/test_golden_chain_composition.py::test_missing_import_rejected_by_real_mypy`. It passes at dev 3102bd1c11. With the product change of 2f356ffc6688 reverted at dev, it fails because the run ends `rejected_handler_test`, not `rejected_typecheck`.\n- AC2: the orchestrator, validator and mypy-effect suites. Result: 74 passed, 1 skipped at dev 3102bd1c11. This is a non-regression criterion that predates the change.\n\nThe commit carries the merged-fix trailer naming 2f356ffc6688. `git diff <fix>^1 <fix> -- src/ | git apply -R --check` succeeds at dev.\n\nLab: host=launching Mac (focused checks, not lab-placed), command=`uv run pytest <the AC1 node> plus the two OMN-21151 golden-chain nodes -q` => 3 passed in 7.06s, and the AC2 suite command => 74 passed, 1 skipped in 11.97s, head=3102bd1c11d4d65dbf5bd266bb410ddb63ddf5c2. This PR's repo-evidence / dod-verify run re-executes each bound check at the PR head.\n",
